-    "body": "<p>The vendor dashboard calendar shows that vendor’s unpaid linked-line allocations, summed by due date; choose a calendar item to manage its payment. The separate Calendar tab shows budget-wide daily planned totals and can include paid history or incoming funding. Undated payments do not appear on either calendar.</p><p>In Downloads choose <b>One calendar month</b> or <b>From / To dates</b>. PDF and .ics use the same inclusive boundaries, payment scope and history setting. Include paid payments, refunds &amp; received funding to include history. Undated entries cannot be plotted; expected refunds remain forecast incoming items.</p><p>PDF creates a page for each touched month with additional detail pages for crowded dates. A PDF range is limited to 10 years; .ics can cover longer ranges. Empty ranges produce no invented events. Calendar-view buttons use its displayed month; Custom date range… opens Downloads.</p><p>Import .ics into a new dedicated Apple/Google calendar. For an updated snapshot, delete only that old dedicated calendar and import into a new one. There is no live sync; the app does not create/delete external calendars. Live import on your calendar service still needs verification.</p>"
+    "body": "<p>The Calendar tab displays scoped daily due totals. Select Week, Month, Year, Max or inclusive From / To dates; this same range and the selected history/filter settings control PDF, CSV and .ics downloads on this screen. Week, Month and Year use the current calendar period; Max spans the earliest to latest dated transaction, or the current month if none. Today returns to the current month. The outlined day is today. Scroll through months inside the selected range; select View details or + more to see all entries on crowded days. Outgoing and incoming arrows identify direction; green denotes paid/received and yellow denotes past-due unpaid amounts. Undated items cannot appear.</p><p>The contact dashboard has a separate scrollable calendar of that contact’s linked-line transactions and a Today button. Shared transactions show only linked-line allocations. Downloads also has its own calendar date controls. PDF ranges are limited to ten years; CSV and .ics can cover longer ranges.</p><p>.ics is an import-once snapshot, not synchronization. First create a new dedicated calendar in Apple Calendar (File → New Calendar) or Google Calendar (Settings → Add calendar → Create new calendar), then import the file into it. For a replacement snapshot, remove only the old dedicated calendar and import into another new one. The app does not create or delete external calendars; real-device imports need verification.</p>"
